+    This file provides support disassembly ( arm ).
+
+    Windows NT runs ARM code in the Thumb instruction set alone (Thumb-2):
+    16-bit instructions and 32-bit ones of two halfwords, the first halfword
+    0xe800 or above, with the VFP and Advanced SIMD instructions. They are
+    written in the unified assembler language of ARM. An instruction in an
+    IT block takes its condition from the IT instruction before it, when the
+    instructions are disassembled one after the other.
